%T A400336 6245592,27766356,126655587,594304478,2856477276,14067444809,
%U A400336 70825304205,364431566684,1913624230478,10249781177456,55938551639995,310916074576073,1758452762795238,10115290437316352
%N A400336 Number of partial matchings of n points on a circle up to rotation and reflection.
%C A400336 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of orbits of the involutions of Z_n = {0, 1, ..., n-1} under conjugation by the dihedral group generated by i -> i+1 and i -> -i; i.e., the number of partial chord diagrams on a bracelet of n points, where points may be left unmatched and chords may cross.
%C A400336 a(n) is also the number of side-pairing patterns of an n-gon up to rotation and reflection of the n-gon: each side is either glued to itself by a half-turn about its midpoint or glued to one other side by an orientation-preserving map.
%C A400336 Perfect matchings (n even, no fixed points) up to rotation and reflection are counted by A054499(n/2).
%C A400336 A400335(n) - a(n) is the number of chiral pairs of patterns and 2*a(n) - A400335(n) the number of patterns equivalent to their mirror image.
%D A400336 a(n) = (A400335(n) + R(n))/2, where R(n) = A000898((n-1)/2) for odd n and R(n) = A000898(n/2-1) + A000898(n/2)/2 for even n.
%D A400336 (Burnside's lemma: a reflection of Z_n with f fixed points and t 2-cycles commutes with A000085(f)*A000898(t) involutions; for odd n every reflection has f = 1, for even n half of the reflections have f = 2 and half have f = 0.)
%D A400336 a(n) = (1/(2*n))*(Sum_{d|n} phi(n/d)*F(d, n/d) + n*A000898((n-1)/2)) for odd n; a(n) = (1/(2*n))*(Sum_{d|n} phi(n/d)*F(d, n/d) + (n/2)*(2*A000898(n/2-1) + A000898(n/2))) for even n; where F(g, L) = Sum_{k=0..floor(g/2)} g!/((g-2*k)!*k!*2^k) * L^k * s^(g-2*k), with s = 2 if L is even and s = 1 if L is odd.
%H A400336 Rasmus Joergensen, <a href="/A400336/b400336.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..200</a>
%e A400336 a(6) = 17: of the A400335(6) = 18 classes up to rotation, the classes of (0 1)(2 4) and (0 1)(3 5) are exchanged by the reflection i -> 1-i and are not related by a rotation; the other 16 classes are mapped to themselves.
%o A400336 (Python)
%o A400336 from math import gcd, factorial
%o A400336 def F(g, L):
%o A400336     # involutions commuting with a permutation that has g cycles of length L
%o A400336     s = 2 if L % 2 == 0 else 1
%o A400336     return sum(factorial(g)//(factorial(g-2*p)*factorial(p)*2**p)*L**p*s**(g-2*p) for p in range(g//2+1))
%o A400336 def a(n):
%o A400336     rot = sum(F(gcd(n, r), n//gcd(n, r)) for r in range(n))
%o A400336     if n % 2: ref = n*F((n-1)//2, 2)
%o A400336     else: ref = n//2*(2*F(n//2-1, 2) + F(n//2, 2))
%o A400336     return (rot + ref)//(2*n)
%Y A400336 Cf. A000085, A000898, A007769, A054499, A400335.
%K A400336 nonn,new
%O A400336 1,2
%A A400336 _Rasmus Joergensen_, Sep 23 2026
